@rem Exercises for lesson 04_exam_tips (C track). Format: docs/CONTENT_FORMAT.md

@exercise c-exam-choice-compile
@type choice
@lesson 04_exam_tips
@difficulty 1
@prompt
Four of your five functions are correct, but the file has a compile error. What is the result?
@choices
- 80 percent
- 4 out of 5 functions are marked
* 0 for the whole exam
- Only the broken function gets 0
@explain
A compile error, an infinite loop or a crash gives 0 for the whole exam.

@exercise c-exam-choice-wrong
@type choice
@lesson 04_exam_tips
@difficulty 1
@prompt
One function compiles and finishes but returns a wrong result. What happens?
@choices
* Only that function fails
- The whole exam gets 0
- The file is not marked
- All functions after it fail
@explain
A wrong result fails only that function.

@exercise c-exam-choice-unfinished
@type choice
@lesson 04_exam_tips
@difficulty 1
@prompt
You cannot finish a function in time. What is the safest thing to do?
@choices
- Leave the half-written loop in the file
- Delete the function from the file
* Make it compile and terminate with a placeholder return value
- Comment out the tests at the bottom
@explain
A function that compiles and ends can at worst fail by itself. Half a loop can break the build or never end, and then the whole exam is 0.
